tal": 137268, "input": 2827, "output": 98, "reasoning": 711, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 133632}}, "modelID": "mimo-v2.6-flash-free", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1793037127806, "completed": 1793037158221}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_17957507e001g1jVqR8gODZ5uJ", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_179575f13001dgPidSopVLbjS9", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957507e001g1jVqR8gODZ5uJ"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user wants: \"встрой в html и отправь на гитхаб и сюда я скачаю и протестирую на телефоне\" — embed into the HTML and push to GitHub, and put it \"here\" (in tmp for download via Files tab) so they can download and test on the phone.\n\nThe koma-web.html is already self-contained (10MB, with onnxruntime embedded, models loaded via IndexedDB through the models sheet — user uploads detection.onnx, cyrillic.onnx, cyrillic.txt manually via the UI). Wait — the models are stored via file upload in the UI (storeModelFiles). So for the phone test, the user needs:\n1. koma-web.html (patched — already committed on the branch)\n2. The three model files\n\n\"встрой в html\" — maybe they want the models embedded into the HTML too? That would make it truly self-contained for phone use. Let me check how embeddedDictText works and whether there's a pattern for embedding models. Line 2225: async function embeddedDictText(). Let me look at that area to see if there's an existing embedding mechanism (part0-dict.js was in the build). The dict is already embedded. Models (13MB total) are not.\n\n\"встрой в html\" most likely means: make the final single-file HTML with everything needed (including the models so they don't have to upload them manually on the phone), OR just \"embed the fix into the html\" (the fix is already in koma-web.html). Given the context — \"и сюда я скачаю и протестирую на телефоне\" — they want a downloadable artifact. The simplest interpretation: put the patched koma-web.html + models into tmp (Files tab) and push to GitHub (already on the branch; maybe also merge to main? or create a release with assets).\n\nCreating a GitHub release with the html + models attached would let them download on the phone easily. Also copy to /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp for the Files tab.\n\nShould I merge the PR to main? The user said \"отправь на гитхаб\" — it's already pushed to the branch and PR is open. For phone testing they can download from the release or from the branch raw URL. Let me:\n\n1. Check embeddedDictText to understand the embedding pattern.\n2. Consider embedding models as base64 in the HTML — 13MB → ~18MB base64, HTML would be ~30MB. That's heavy but works offline without manual upload. Let me see if the existing code auto-loads embedded models. Check line 2225 and around 2640.\n\nActually, let me look at how models load on startup (line 5762-5782 earlier: `const det = await DB.get('kv', 'model:det')` ... `if (!ok && (await DB.get('kv','model:det'))) toast(...)`). So models must be in IndexedDB, uploaded via UI. If I embed models in the HTML as base64 and auto-seed IndexedDB on first run, the phone test becomes: download one file, open, import manga, scan. That's the best interpretation of \"встрой в html\".\n\nLet me check embeddedDictText for the pattern.", "time": {"start": 1793037131540, "end": 1793037156018}, "id": "prt_179575f14001soqygBca2k1y8i", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957507e001g1jVqR8gODZ5uJ"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_389f9f8392474b3ab7c1437e", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code && sed -n '2218,2250p' koma-web.html; echo ===; sed -n '2630,2660p' koma-web.html; echo ===; sed -n '5762,5789p' koma-web.html"}, "output": "...output truncated...\n\nFull output saved to: /home/runner/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_17957c6da001F02J1wOo1We254\n\nhmFcJ053Jxn/IqMe9IiP+3CPztJtTuZZtrq1g9fUzYoeCw49wtulxurbr9P8DRzv+OXiqTAA=';\n\n/** Разжать вшитый словарь и отдать текстом (построчно, «слово частота»). */\nasync function embeddedDictText() {\n  const bytes = b64ToBytes(DICT_GZ_B64);\n  if (typeof DecompressionStream === 'undefined') {\n    throw new Error('браузер не умеет DecompressionStream');\n  }\n  const buf = await new Response(\n    new Blob([bytes]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip'))\n  ).arrayBuffer();\n  return new TextDecoder('utf-8').decode(new Uint8Array(buf));\n}\n'use strict';\n/* ───────────────────────── 0. Мелкие утилиты ───────────────────────── */\nconst $ = (s) => document.querySelector(s);\nconst $$ = (s) => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(s));\nconst clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\nfunction toast(msg, ms = 2200) {\n  const el = $('#toast');\n  el.textContent = msg; el.classList.add('on');\n  clearTimeout(toast._t);\n  toast._t = setTimeout(() => el.classList.remove('on'), ms);\n}\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));\n\nconst VERSION = 'v1.9.11';\n\n/* ───────────────────────── 1. Хранилище (IndexedDB) ─────────────────────────\n===\n  ALPHABET: 'абвгдежзийклмнопрстуфхцчшщъыьэюяё'.split(''),\n  source: '',\n  async load() {\n    // 1) Свой файл, если пользователь загрузил его кнопкой «Словарь ru_250k»\n    //    (нужен, если вшитый не подошёл). 2) Иначе — вшитый в файл словарь.\n    let text = '';\n    const row = await DB.get('kv', 'dict:ru250k');\n    if (row && row.v) { text = String(row.v); this.source = 'свой файл'; }\n    else if (typeof DICT_GZ_B64 === 'string' && DICT_GZ_B64.length > 1000) {\n      try {\n        text = await embeddedDictText();\n        this.source = 'вшит в файл';\n      } catch (e) {\n        console.warn('вшитый словарь не разжался:', e);\n      }\n    }\n    if (!text) { this.ready = false; return false; }\n    const lines = text.split('\\n');\n    const rank = new Map();\n    let n = 0;\n    for (const line of lines) {\n      const w = line.split(/\\s+/)[0];\n      if (!w) continue;\n      const low = w.toLowerCase();\n      if (!rank.has(low)) rank.set(low, n);\n      n++;\n    }\n    this.rank = rank; this.size = n; this.ready = n > 1000;\n    return this.ready;\n  },\n  /** Слово верное, если оно из частых. */\n===\n  const det = await DB.get('kv', 'model:det');\n  const parts = [];\n  parts.push('OCR: ' + OCR.statusText());\n  parts.push('словарь: ' + (Words.ready ? Words.size.toLocaleString('ru-RU') + ' слов (' + (Words.source || 'вшит') + ')' : 'не загрузился'));\n  parts.push(typeof ort === 'undefined' ? 'onnxruntime-web не загружен (нужна сеть)' : 'onnxruntime-web загружен');\n  parts.push('TTS ' + (speechSynthesis.getVoices().length ? 'есть' : 'нет голосов'));\n  if (ENV.android) parts.push('Android: папки нет, выбирайте файлы/CBZ');\n  $('#selfCheck').textContent = 'KOMA Web ' + VERSION + ' · ' + parts.join(' · ');\n}\n\n(async function boot() {\n  bindUI();\n  Words.load().catch(e => console.warn('словарь не загрузился', e));\n  watchScroll();\n  TTS.init();\n  const saved = await DB.get('kv', 'rules');\n  if (saved) { try { RULES = sanitizeRules(JSON.parse(saved.v)); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); } }\n  await Library.load();\n  await renderModels();\n  const ok = await OCR.loadModels().catch(e => { console.warn('модели не загрузились', e); return false; });\n  if (!ok && (await DB.get('kv', 'model:det'))) toast('Модели есть, но движок не загрузился — нужна сеть для onnxruntime-web', 5000);\n  renderRulesInfo();\n  showEnvBanner();\n  await selfCheck();\n  setTimeout(selfCheck, 2500);\n  // предупреждение о среде\n  if (typeof ort === 'undefined') {\n    $('#ortState').textContent = 'onnxruntime-web не загрузился: нет сети или открыто в предпросмотре без интернета.';\n", "metadata": {"output": "...\n\';\n\n/** Разжать вшитый словарь и отдать текстом (построчно, «слово частота»). */\nasync function embeddedDictText() {\n  const bytes = b64ToBytes(DICT_GZ_B64);\n  if (typeof DecompressionStream === 'undefined') {\n    throw new Error('браузер не умеет DecompressionStream');\n  }\n  const buf = await new Response(\n    new Blob([bytes]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip'))\n  ).arrayBuffer();\n  return new TextDecoder('utf-8').decode(new Uint8Array(buf));\n}\n'use strict';\n/* ───────────────────────── 0. Мелкие утилиты ───────────────────────── */\nconst $ = (s) => document.querySelector(s);\nconst $$ = (s) => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(s));\nconst clamp = (v, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\nfunction toast(msg, ms = 2200) {\n  const el = $('#toast');\n  el.textContent = msg; el.classList.add('on');\n  clearTimeout(toast._t);\n  toast._t = setTimeout(() => el.classList.remove('on'), ms);\n}\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));\n\nconst VERSION = 'v1.9.11';\n\n/* ───────────────────────── 1. Хранилище (IndexedDB) ─────────────────────────\n===\n  ALPHABET: 'абвгдежзийклмнопрстуфхцчшщъыьэюяё'.split(''),\n  source: '',\n  async load() {\n    // 1) Свой файл, если пользователь загрузил его кнопкой «Словарь ru_250k»\n    //    (нужен, если вшитый не подошёл). 2) Иначе — вшитый в файл словарь.\n    let text = '';\n    const row = await DB.get('kv', 'dict:ru250k');\n    if (row && row.v) { text = String(row.v); this.source = 'свой файл'; }\n    else if (typeof DICT_GZ_B64 === 'string' && DICT_GZ_B64.length > 1000) {\n      try {\n        text = await embeddedDictText();\n        this.source = 'вшит в файл';\n      } catch (e) {\n        console.warn('вшитый словарь не разжался:', e);\n      }\n    }\n    if (!text) { this.ready = false; return false; }\n    const lines = text.split('\\n');\n    const rank = new Map();\n    let n = 0;\n    for (const line of lines) {\n      const w = line.split(/\\s+/)[0];\n      if (!w) continue;\n      const low = w.toLowerCase();\n      if (!rank.has(low)) rank.set(low, n);\n      n++;\n    }\n    this.rank = rank; this.size = n; this.ready = n > 1000;\n    return this.ready;\n  },\n  /** Слово верное, если оно из частых. */\n===\n  const det = await DB.get('kv', 'model:det');\n  const parts = [];\n  parts.push('OCR: ' + OCR.statusText());\n  parts.push('словарь: ' + (Words.ready ? Words.size.toLocaleString('ru-RU') + ' слов (' + (Words.source || 'вшит') + ')' : 'не загрузился'));\n  parts.push(typeof ort === 'undefined' ? 'onnxruntime-web не загружен (нужна сеть)' : 'onnxruntime-web загружен');\n  parts.push('TTS ' + (speechSynthesis.getVoices().length ? 'есть' : 'нет голосов'));\n  if (ENV.android) parts.push('Android: папки нет, выбирайте файлы/CBZ');\n  $('#selfCheck').textContent = 'KOMA Web ' + VERSION + ' · ' + parts.join(' · ');\n}\n\n(async function boot() {\n  bindUI();\n  Words.load().catch(e => console.warn('словарь не загрузился', e));\n  watchScroll();\n  TTS.init();\n  const saved = await DB.get('kv', 'rules');\n  if (saved) { try { RULES = sanitizeRules(JSON.parse(saved.v)); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); } }\n  await Library.load();\n  await renderModels();\n  const ok = await OCR.loadModels().catch(e => { console.warn('модели не загрузились', e); return false; });\n  if (!ok && (await DB.get('kv', 'model:det'))) toast('Модели есть, но движок не загрузился — нужна сеть для onnxruntime-web', 5000);\n  renderRulesInfo();\n  showEnvBanner();\n  await selfCheck();\n  setTimeout(selfCheck, 2500);\n  // предупреждение о среде\n  if (typeof ort === 'undefined') {\n    $('#ortState').textContent = 'onnxruntime-web не загрузился: нет сети или открыто в предпросмотре без интернета.';\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": true, "outputPath": "/home/runner/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_17957c6da001F02J1wOo1We254"}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code && sed -n '2218,2250p' koma-web.html; echo ===; sed -n '2630,2660p' koma-web.html; echo ===; sed -n '5762,5789p' koma-web.html", "time": {"start": 1793037158087, "end": 1793037158165}}, "id": "prt_17957beb7001DGyTFjTXWSo0ii", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957507e001g1jVqR8gODZ5uJ"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 137268, "input": 2827, "output": 98, "reasoning": 711, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 133632}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_17957c740001ARTllpI9wfmz31", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957507e001g1jVqR8gODZ5uJ"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1795613e5001EpPzsEUAJPtRZK", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 140144, "input": 2060, "output": 138, "reasoning": 1498, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 136448}}, "modelID": "mimo-v2.6-flash-free", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1793037158320, "completed": 1793037209725}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_17957c7b0001H9u4y20fuBK7lX", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_17957e0b1001mPRn6KFpx6kEaK", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957c7b0001H9u4y20fuBK7lX"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user wants: \"встрой в html и отправь на гитхаб и сюда я скачаю и протестирую на телефоне\" — embed into html and send to github and here (tmp folder) so they can download and test on the phone.\n\nThe html is already self-contained (10MB, contains onnxruntime + embedded dict). Models (detection.onnx, cyrillic.onnx, cyrillic.txt) are loaded via IndexedDB from the Models sheet — the user uploads them manually on the phone. So the deliverable is:\n\n1. The patched `koma-web.html` (already committed on branch fix/title-line-crop).\n2. Copy it to `/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/` for download via the Files tab.\n3. Maybe also attach to a GitHub release for easy download on the phone.\n\n\"встрой в html\" — maybe they mean embed the models into the html too? The html is 10MB already; embedding models would make it ~25MB (detection 4.7MB + cyrillic 7.9MB + dict already embedded). That would make it truly single-file for phone testing — no need to upload models manually. Let me check how the models are loaded: `OCR.loadModels` reads from IndexedDB `model:det`, `model:rec`, `model:dict`. On first run, user must import the three files via the sheet.\n\nEmbedding models as base64 into the html would add ~17MB of base64 (12.6MB binary → ~17MB base64). The html would become ~27MB. On a phone that's fine to open as a local file.\n\nBut wait — \"встрой в html\" might just mean \"embed the fix into the html\" (already done — the patch is in koma-web.html). Given previous context, the user may simply want the final html ready to download and test. But to be safe and maximally useful: create a self-contained build with models embedded, so on the phone they just open the file and it works without uploading models.\n\nLet me look at how boot handles models — if DB has no model:det, renderModels shows missing state; user must pick files. If I embed models as base64 constants (like DICT_GZ_B64), I need to add loading logic. Let me check if there's already support for embedded models... grep for EMBED or similar in the html. There's `embeddedDictText` for the dict only. So I'd need to add an embedded-models path.\n\nPlan:\n1. Add to koma-web.html (on the branch): `EMBEDDED_MODELS` support — b64 constants for detection.onnx and cyrillic.onnx (maybe gzip+base64 to shrink; onnx files may not compress much... let me check. Actually ONNX files are protobuf with float weights — gzip might help ~30-40%? Let me test).\n2. In boot, if `model:det` missing and embedded models present, auto-seed IndexedDB from the embedded bytes.\n3. Rebuild/patch html, commit, push, create a release with the html attached (so phone can download easily), and copy to tmp.\n\nSize concern: html is already 10MB (onnxruntime embedded). Adding 12.6MB binary → base64 17MB → total ~27MB. gzip might reduce: let me test compression ratio quickly.\n\nActually, wait. The user said \"встрой в html\" — could also mean \"embed [the fix] into html\" i.e., make sure the fix is in the html file (not just scripts in tmp). The koma-web.html on the branch already has the fix. But \"и сюда я скачаю\" — put it in tmp for download. And \"протестирую на телефоне\" — test on phone. On the phone, they'd need models too. The previous flow (e2e) shows models are imported via UI. If they test on phone they'd need to upload the3 model files — annoying but doable. Embedding makes it seamless.\n\nI'll go with embedding models into the html — it's the most useful interpretation (\"self-contained build for phone testing\"). Keep the embedded models optional: if constants exist and DB empty → seed. Also add a way to clear? The models sheet already has delete. Fine.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Models: detection.onnx (4.7MB), cyrillic.onnx (7.9MB). Base64 → +33%. Total html ~27-28MB. That's large but OK for a local file. Could gzip: check ratio.\n\nLet me test gzip ratio on the onnx files.\n\nAlso loading a 28MB html on a phone browser — fine.\n\nSteps:\n1. Test gzip compression on models.\n2. Write a Python script that generates a JS snippet with base64 constants (gzipped if beneficial) and patches koma-web.html: insert constants near DICT_GZ_B64 and add boot seeding logic.\n3. Modify boot: after Library.load, before renderModels/OCR.loadModels: if !model:det && typeof EMBED_DET_B64 === 'string' → decode, put to DB (also rec, dict).\n4. Commit on the branch, push.\n5. Create GitHub release (tag v1.9.11-fix1 or similar) attaching the html — phone can download from release. Or just push the file to the branch; user can download raw from GitHub. A release asset is easier: `gh release create`.\n6. Copy final html to /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/koma-web.html for the Files tab download.\n7. Quick sanity test in chromium: open the new html fresh (clear IndexedDB), check engine ready without uploading models, run the band scan once to verify \"будучи\".\n\nWait — the phone also needs onnxruntime-web: it's already embedded in the html (10MB includes ort). Good. And the dict is embedded. So the html alone would be fully self-contained.\n\nOne concern: seeding12MB into IndexedDB on every boot when missing — fine, once.\n\nAlso `renderModels` before seeding? Order in boot: Library.load → renderModels → OCR.loadModels. I'll seed right before renderModels.\n\nLet me check where DICT_GZ_B64 is defined and what surrounds it, to insert EMBED constants nearby. The dict b64 ends around line 2218-2220. I'll append after embeddedDictText.\n\nAlso need b64ToBytes — exists already (used by embeddedDictText).\n\nGzip: let me measure. If gzipped ratio is good (~60-70% of base64 original), embed gzipped and decompress with DecompressionStream like the dict. Fallback: if DecompressionStream missing (old browsers), skip seeding (models can still be uploaded manually). Chrome on phone supports it.\n\nLet me do it.", "time": {"start": 1793037164723, "end": 1793037206226}, "id": "prt_17957e0b3001efQyhoRvBohP5W", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957c7b0001H9u4y20fuBK7lX"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_c79b46f9f30c451589e6f1b6", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/models && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport gzip, os, base64\nfor f in ['detection.onnx','cyrillic.onnx','cyrillic.txt']:\n    raw=open(f,'rb').read()\n    gz=gzip.compress(raw,9)\n    print(f, 'raw', len(raw), 'gz', len(gz), 'ratio %.2f'%(len(gz)/len(raw)), 'b64gz', len(base64.b64encode(gz)))\nPY"}, "output": "detection.onnx raw 4745517 gz 4386403 ratio 0.92 b64gz 5848540\ncyrillic.onnx raw 7870092 gz 7297744 ratio 0.93 b64gz 9730328\ncyrillic.txt raw 1663 gz 1082 ratio 0.65 b64gz 1444\n", "metadata": {"output": "detection.onnx raw 4745517 gz 4386403 ratio 0.92 b64gz 5848540\ncyrillic.onnx raw 7870092 gz 7297744 ratio 0.93 b64gz 9730328\ncyrillic.txt raw 1663 gz 1082 ratio 0.65 b64gz 1444\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/models && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport gzip, os, base64\nfor f in ['detection.onnx','cyrillic.onnx','cyrillic.txt']:\n    raw=open(f,'rb').read()\n    gz=gzip.compress(raw,9)\n    print(f, 'raw', len(raw), 'gz', len(gz), 'ratio %.2f'%(len(gz)/len(raw)), 'b64gz', len(base64.b64encode(gz)))\nPY", "time": {"start": 1793037209205, "end": 1793037209702}}, "id": "prt_1795882d3001EkDkQXt1Vy1wJY", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957c7b0001H9u4y20fuBK7lX"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 140144, "input": 2060, "output": 138, "reasoning": 1498, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 136448}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_179589072001e0Xm66zmVOjgja", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17957c7b0001H9u4y20fuBK7lX"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1795613e5001EpPzsEUAJPtRZK", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 140543, "input": 1770, "output": 85, "reasoning": 192, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 138496}}, "modelID": "mimo-v2.6-flash-free", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1793037209815, "completed": 1793037221108}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1795890d7001O3c6n9h7QXR5p3", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_17958a582001bS0xBD3RLvD14D", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795890d7001O3c6n9h7QXR5p3"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The models are ~12.6 MB. Embedding them as base64 would make the HTML ~28 MB. The user says \"встрой в html\" — embed into html. They want to download and test on phone. The dict is already embedded (DICT_GZ_B64). Models are loaded from IndexedDB via the models sheet. For phone testing, the user would need the models too. Let me check what \"встрой\" means — probably embed the models into the HTML so it's fully self-contained for phone testing.\n\n28 MB HTML is large but works on phone (local file). Alternatively they just want the current koma-web.html (already has the fix) + models files. But user explicitly said \"встрой в html\" — embed into the html.\n\nLet me check if there's already an embedded-models mechanism. Look for how boot loads models and if there's an EMBED placeholder.", "time": {"start": 1793037215108, "end": 1793037219841}, "id": "prt_17958a584001825Tu78QWUHixS", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795890d7001O3c6n9h7QXR5p3"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_7798a0fb13834e9c917df525", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code && grep -n \"DICT_GZ_B64\\|MODEL.*B64\\|EMBED\" koma-web.html | head; echo ===; sed -n '5100,5135p' koma-web.html"}, "output": "...output truncated...\n\nFull output saved to: /home/runner/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_17958bc74001UjpMsMfIfELpxr\n\n  u.onstart = () => { started = true; };\n  u.onerror = (e) => { err = (e && e.error) || 'unknown'; };\n  try {\n    if (speechSynthesis.speaking || speechSynthesis.pending) speechSynthesis.cancel();\n    speechSynthesis.speak(u);\n  } catch (e) {\n    parts.push('система не приняла фразу: ' + (e.message || e));\n    return parts.join(' · ');\n  }\n  await sleep(1500);\n  parts.push(started ? 'синтез заговорил' : (err ? 'ошибка синтеза: ' + err : 'синтез не ответил за 1,5 с'));\n  return parts.join(' · ');\n}\n\nasync function selfTestEngine() {\n  if (!OCR.ready) {\n    const ok = await OCR.loadModels().catch(e => { OCR.engine = 'failed'; OCR.reason = String(e.message || e); return false; });\n    if (!ok) { await renderModels(); toast(OCR.statusText() + (OCR.reason ? ': ' + OCR.reason : ''), 8000); return; }\n  }\n  try {\n    // Тестовая «страница» рисуется НАСТОЯЩИМ canvas: у элемента нет свойства\n    // .data (оно было только в Node-заглушке), из-за этого проверка падала с\n    // «Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'length')».\n    const W = 600, H = 800;\n    const c = makeCanvas(W, H);\n    const ctx = c.getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true });\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#101010';\n    for (let y = 120; y < 180; y += 2) ctx.fillRect(80, y, 440, 1);\n    const boxes = await detectBoxes(c, DEFAULT_RULES.pageSide, RULES);\n    toast(boxes.length\n      ? 'Движок считает: детектор вернул ' + boxes.length + ' бокс(ов) на тестовой картинке'\n      : 'Движок считает, но на тестовой картинке боксов 0 — проверьте модели', 7000);\n    await renderModels();\n  } catch (e) {\n", "metadata": {"output": "...\n\';\n2226:  const bytes = b64ToBytes(DICT_GZ_B64);\n2638:    else if (typeof DICT_GZ_B64 === 'string' && DICT_GZ_B64.length > 1000) {\n===\n  u.onstart = () => { started = true; };\n  u.onerror = (e) => { err = (e && e.error) || 'unknown'; };\n  try {\n    if (speechSynthesis.speaking || speechSynthesis.pending) speechSynthesis.cancel();\n    speechSynthesis.speak(u);\n  } catch (e) {\n    parts.push('система не приняла фразу: ' + (e.message || e));\n    return parts.join(' · ');\n  }\n  await sleep(1500);\n  parts.push(started ? 'синтез заговорил' : (err ? 'ошибка синтеза: ' + err : 'синтез не ответил за 1,5 с'));\n  return parts.join(' · ');\n}\n\nasync function selfTestEngine() {\n  if (!OCR.ready) {\n    const ok = await OCR.loadModels().catch(e => { OCR.engine = 'failed'; OCR.reason = String(e.message || e); return false; });\n    if (!ok) { await renderModels(); toast(OCR.statusText() + (OCR.reason ? ': ' + OCR.reason : ''), 8000); return; }\n  }\n  try {\n    // Тестовая «страница» рисуется НАСТОЯЩИМ canvas: у элемента нет свойства\n    // .data (оно было только в Node-заглушке), из-за этого проверка падала с\n    // «Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'length')».\n    const W = 600, H = 800;\n    const c = makeCanvas(W, H);\n    const ctx = c.getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true });\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#101010';\n    for (let y = 120; y < 180; y += 2) ctx.fillRect(80, y, 440, 1);\n    const boxes = await detectBoxes(c, DEFAULT_RULES.pageSide, RULES);\n    toast(boxes.length\n      ? 'Движок считает: детектор вернул ' + boxes.length + ' бокс(ов) на тестовой картинке'\n      : 'Движок считает, но на тестовой картинке боксов 0 — проверьте модели', 7000);\n    await renderModels();\n  } catch (e) {\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": true, "outputPath": "/home/runner/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_17958bc74001UjpMsMfIfELpxr"}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code && grep -n \"DICT_GZ_B64\\|MODEL.*B64\\|EMBED\" koma-web.html | head; echo ===; sed -n '5100,5135p' koma-web.html", "time": {"start": 1793037220947, "end": 1793037221059}}, "id": "prt_17958b8030012m4ySC8c3CFc16", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795890d7001O3c6n9h7QXR5p3"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 140543, "input": 1770, "output": 85, "reasoning": 192, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 138496}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_17958bce5001gmwLD5yLsKQv7W", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795890d7001O3c6n9h7QXR5p3"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1795613e5001EpPzsEUAJPtRZK", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code