one (since on phone they'd otherwise need to manually import detection.onnx/cyrillic.onnx/cyrillic.txt via the UI).\n\nLet me check the structure: DICT_GZ_B64 is already embedded (the dictionary). Models are stored in IndexedDB via UI file upload. To make the phone test seamless, I should embed the ONNX models as base64 gzip into the HTML and auto-seed IndexedDB on first boot if models are missing.\n\nModel sizes: detection.onnx 4.7MB gz→4.4MB b64→5.8MB; cyrillic.onnx 7.9MB gz→7.3MB b64→9.7MB. Total added ~15.5MB to the HTML (currently 10MB →25.5MB). That's big but acceptable for a single-file test build. The user explicitly asked \"встрой в html\" — embed into html.\n\nPlan:\n1. Generate a JS snippet with EMBED_DET_GZ_B64, EMBED_REC_GZ_B64 (and dict is already there).\n2. Add auto-seed logic: in boot, if DB lacks model:det, decode embedded models and store into IndexedDB, then load.\n3. Build a separate artifact: don't necessarily commit the 15MB of base64 into git? The user said \"отправь на гитхаб\" — push to GitHub. The PR branch already has the fix. They want the built HTML for phone testing — \"и сюда я скачаю\" — put it in tmp/ for download via Files tab.\n\nOptions: commit the embedded-models version to the repo would bloat git history massively (15MB). Better: keep the code change (embedding hooks) minimal in the repo? Actually the user just wants a testable file. I'll create the embedded HTML as a build artifact in tmp/ (koma-web-bundled.html) AND push the embedding logic to the branch? Hmm — \"встрой в html и отправь на гитхаб\" — embed into html and send to GitHub. Simplest interpretation: produce the final HTML with models embedded, push it to GitHub (maybe as a release asset or in the repo), and also copy to tmp for download.\n\nCommitting a 25MB file into the repo is ugly. Better: create a GitHub release with the HTML attached. gh release create with the file. That gives a download link for the phone. And copy to /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/koma-web-bundled.html for the Files tab.\n\nAlso the embedding code: I can generate the bundled HTML by injecting base64 constants + auto-seed into the current koma-web.html without committing the huge base64 to the repo. But then the repo version wouldn't be the bundled one — fine, the release asset is the bundle. Actually simpler: write a small build script in tmp that takes code/koma-web.html and produces tmp/koma-web-bundled.html with embedded models. The HTML itself doesn't need repo changes for auto-seed if... wait, it does — the boot must know to seed from embedded constants. I need to add the auto-seed logic to koma-web.html in the repo (small), then the bundler script just appends/injects the big base64 constants.\n\nLet me look at the boot/model loading code to add seeding.", "time": {"start": 1793037247259, "end": 1793037271253}, "id": "prt_17959231a0012bryQkgZH5OuvV", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795915bb001pS12Na9gNGGT0P"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00b09026caa448cea6b7c432", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code && sed -n '2880,2960p' koma-web.html"}, "output": "    return '';\n  },\n};\n\n/* ───────────────────────── 5. OCR: модели в браузере ───────────────────────── */\nconst OCR = {\n  det: null, rec: null, dict: null, ready: false,\n  // Честное состояние движка. Раньше интерфейс писал «движок загружен,\n  // моделей нет» даже когда все три модели лежали на месте, — потому что\n  // флага было всего два. Теперь видно, на каком шаге и почему всё встало.\n  engine: 'idle',        // idle | loading | ready | blocked | failed\n  reason: '',\n  hasFiles() { return !!(this.pendingDet && this.pendingRec && this.pendingDict); },\n  async loadModels() {\n    const det = await DB.get('kv', 'model:det');\n    const rec = await DB.get('kv', 'model:rec');\n    const dict = await DB.get('kv', 'model:dict');\n    this.pendingDet = !!det; this.pendingRec = !!rec; this.pendingDict = !!dict;\n    if (!det || !rec || !dict) {\n      this.ready = false; this.engine = 'idle';\n      this.reason = 'моделей нет';\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (typeof ort === 'undefined') {\n      this.ready = false; this.engine = 'failed';\n      this.reason = 'onnxruntime-web не загрузился: нужна сеть при первом открытии';\n      return false;\n    }\n    this.engine = 'loading'; this.reason = '';\n    ort.env.wasm.numThreads = 1;                 // без COOP/COEP потоки не нужны\n    ort.env.wasm.simd = true;\n    ort.env.logLevel = 'error';\n    try {\n      // Движок работает на вшитых в файл бинарях: сеть не нужна вообще.\n      await installOrtWasm();\n      this.det = await ort.InferenceSession.create(det.v, { executionProviders: ['wasm'] });\n      this.rec = await ort.InferenceSession.create(rec.v, { executionProviders: ['wasm'] });\n    } catch (e) {\n      this.ready = false;\n      const msg = String((e && e.message) || e);\n      // Песочница/строгий CSP запрещают WebAssembly.instantiate — это среда,\n      // а не файл: на устройстве в Chrome тот же файл работает.\n      const csp = /unsafe-eval|WebAssembly|CompileError|no available backend/i.test(msg);\n      this.engine = csp ? 'blocked' : 'failed';\n      this.reason = csp\n        ? 'WebAssembly запрещён политикой безопасности этой страницы (предпросмотр). '\n          + 'Скачайте файл и откройте в Chrome — там WASM разрешён.'\n        : msg.slice(0, 300);\n      return false;\n    }\n    const lines = String(dict.v).split('\\n');\n    while (lines.length && lines[lines.length - 1] === '') lines.pop();\n    // Ровно как в KomaOcrEngine: blank(0) + символы словаря + пробел.\n    this.dict = [''].concat(lines).concat([' ']);\n    this.ready = true; this.engine = 'ready'; this.reason = '';\n    return true;\n  },\n  /** Короткая строка для интерфейса. */\n  statusText() {\n    if (this.engine === 'ready') return 'движок готов';\n    if (this.engine === 'loading') return 'движок загружается…';\n    if (this.engine === 'blocked') return 'модели есть, но WASM заблокирован этой страницей';\n    if (this.engine === 'failed') return 'модели есть, движок не поднялся';\n    return this.hasFiles() ? 'модели есть, движок не запускался' : 'моделей нет';\n  },\n};\n\n/* ── порог «чернил»: перцентили 2%/98% и коэффициент (KomaOcrEngine.inkThreshold) ── */\nfunction inkThreshold(luma, R) {\n  if (!luma.length) return -1;\n  const hist = new Uint32Array(256);\n  for (let i = 0; i < luma.length; i++) hist[luma[i] | 0]++;\n  const pct = (p) => {\n    const target = Math.max(1, Math.floor(luma.length * p));\n    let acc = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) { acc += hist[i]; if (acc >= target) return i; }\n    return 255;\n  };\n  const low = pct(R.inkLowPercentile), high = pct(R.inkHighPercentile);\n  if (high - low < R.inkFlatSpread) return -1;\n  return clamp(Math.round(low + (high - low) * R.inkCoefficient), R.inkMin, R.inkMax);\n", "metadata": {"output": "    return '';\n  },\n};\n\n/* ───────────────────────── 5. OCR: модели в браузере ───────────────────────── */\nconst OCR = {\n  det: null, rec: null, dict: null, ready: false,\n  // Честное состояние движка. Раньше интерфейс писал «движок загружен,\n  // моделей нет» даже когда все три модели лежали на месте, — потому что\n  // флага было всего два. Теперь видно, на каком шаге и почему всё встало.\n  engine: 'idle',        // idle | loading | ready | blocked | failed\n  reason: '',\n  hasFiles() { return !!(this.pendingDet && this.pendingRec && this.pendingDict); },\n  async loadModels() {\n    const det = await DB.get('kv', 'model:det');\n    const rec = await DB.get('kv', 'model:rec');\n    const dict = await DB.get('kv', 'model:dict');\n    this.pendingDet = !!det; this.pendingRec = !!rec; this.pendingDict = !!dict;\n    if (!det || !rec || !dict) {\n      this.ready = false; this.engine = 'idle';\n      this.reason = 'моделей нет';\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (typeof ort === 'undefined') {\n      this.ready = false; this.engine = 'failed';\n      this.reason = 'onnxruntime-web не загрузился: нужна сеть при первом открытии';\n      return false;\n    }\n    this.engine = 'loading'; this.reason = '';\n    ort.env.wasm.numThreads = 1;                 // без COOP/COEP потоки не нужны\n    ort.env.wasm.simd = true;\n    ort.env.logLevel = 'error';\n    try {\n      // Движок работает на вшитых в файл бинарях: сеть не нужна вообще.\n      await installOrtWasm();\n      this.det = await ort.InferenceSession.create(det.v, { executionProviders: ['wasm'] });\n      this.rec = await ort.InferenceSession.create(rec.v, { executionProviders: ['wasm'] });\n    } catch (e) {\n      this.ready = false;\n      const msg = String((e && e.message) || e);\n      // Песочница/строгий CSP запрещают WebAssembly.instantiate — это среда,\n      // а не файл: на устройстве в Chrome тот же файл работает.\n      const csp = /unsafe-eval|WebAssembly|CompileError|no available backend/i.test(msg);\n      this.engine = csp ? 'blocked' : 'failed';\n      this.reason = csp\n        ? 'WebAssembly запрещён политикой безопасности этой страницы (предпросмотр). '\n          + 'Скачайте файл и откройте в Chrome — там WASM разрешён.'\n        : msg.slice(0, 300);\n      return false;\n    }\n    const lines = String(dict.v).split('\\n');\n    while (lines.length && lines[lines.length - 1] === '') lines.pop();\n    // Ровно как в KomaOcrEngine: blank(0) + символы словаря + пробел.\n    this.dict = [''].concat(lines).concat([' ']);\n    this.ready = true; this.engine = 'ready'; this.reason = '';\n    return true;\n  },\n  /** Короткая строка для интерфейса. */\n  statusText() {\n    if (this.engine === 'ready') return 'движок готов';\n    if (this.engine === 'loading') return 'движок загружается…';\n    if (this.engine === 'blocked') return 'модели есть, но WASM заблокирован этой страницей';\n    if (this.engine === 'failed') return 'модели есть, движок не поднялся';\n    return this.hasFiles() ? 'модели есть, движок не запускался' : 'моделей нет';\n  },\n};\n\n/* ── порог «чернил»: перцентили 2%/98% и коэффициент (KomaOcrEngine.inkThreshold) ── */\nfunction inkThreshold(luma, R) {\n  if (!luma.length) return -1;\n  const hist = new Uint32Array(256);\n  for (let i = 0; i < luma.length; i++) hist[luma[i] | 0]++;\n  const pct = (p) => {\n    const target = Math.max(1, Math.floor(luma.length * p));\n    let acc = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 256; i++) { acc += hist[i]; if (acc >= target) return i; }\n    return 255;\n  };\n  const low = pct(R.inkLowPercentile), high = pct(R.inkHighPercentile);\n  if (high - low < R.inkFlatSpread) return -1;\n  return clamp(Math.round(low + (high - low) * R.inkCoefficient), R.inkMin, R.inkMax);\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code && sed -n '2880,2960p' koma-web.html", "time": {"start": 1793037272653, "end": 1793037272682}}, "id": "prt_1795980d70012ihmXibJV3Vbqs", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795915bb001pS12Na9gNGGT0P"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 142801, "input": 854, "output": 52, "reasoning": 775, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 141120}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_17959867a0017s40dtS9YZPjpW", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795915bb001pS12Na9gNGGT0P"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1795613e5001EpPzsEUAJPtRZK", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 144660, "input": 1970, "output": 78, "reasoning": 660, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 141952}}, "modelID": "mimo-v2.6-flash-free", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1793037272810, "completed": 1793037293027}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1795986ea001L2gEg4Mr1tGGQJ", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_1795992180011Om4U2PN2QOcuy", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795986ea001L2gEg4Mr1tGGQJ"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The user wants: \"встрой в html и отправь на гитхаб и сюда я скачаю и протестирую на телефоне\" — embed into the HTML and send to GitHub, and also here (in tmp for download via Files tab) so they can download and test on the phone.\n\nThe koma-web.html is already self-contained (onnxruntime embedded, dict embedded). Models (detection.onnx, cyrillic.onnx, cyrillic.txt) are stored in IndexedDB via the Models sheet — the user uploads them manually via file picker. The html itself is the deliverable.\n\nSo \"встрой\" likely means: make sure the built html includes the fixes (it already does — we patched koma-web.html directly, which IS the build artifact). The repo's build.sh can't run (missing parts), but koma-web.html is checked in and is the single source.\n\nSo the steps:\n1. The patched koma-web.html is already committed on branch fix/title-line-crop and pushed.\n2. Copy koma-web.html to /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/ for download via Files tab.\n3. Maybe also create a GitHub release with the html attached so the phone can download it easily.\n4. Also copy the model files there so the user can test on phone (they need detection.onnx, cyrillic.onnx, cyrillic.txt to import via the Models sheet).\n\nWait — should we merge the PR to main first? The user said \"отправь на гитхаб\" — send to GitHub. The PR is on GitHub already. But for download convenience, a release is best. Let me create a release on the branch or after merging. Actually merging to main without explicit request... The user said \"пр и комит и продолжай\" earlier — PR and commit. Now \"встрой в html и отправь на гитхаб\" — embed into html and send to github. The html is already patched in the repo. I'll:\n\n1