ml /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/../code/koma-web.html && echo \"html == committed\"", "time": {"start": 1793037292966, "end": 1793037292999}}, "id": "prt_17959cfc9001gTr9qc7BXRk5Km", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795986ea001L2gEg4Mr1tGGQJ"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 144660, "input": 1970, "output": 78, "reasoning": 660, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 141952}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_17959d5d60015XPefC3GI2N2Dk", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_1795986ea001L2gEg4Mr1tGGQJ"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_1795613e5001EpPzsEUAJPtRZK", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 145474, "input": 861, "output": 78, "reasoning": 663, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 143872}}, "modelID": "mimo-v2.6-flash-free", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1793037293133, "completed": 1793037314600}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_17959d64d001yWJgbd6yf6K1EF", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "a77a95e5b6ed5e78c64d830749b6af597f3be05b", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_17959e0360013AF2PFSc2s9Sj1", "sessionID": "ses_e870b7496ffeoaBu30bGkMD4sU", "messageID": "msg_17959d64d001yWJgbd6yf6K1EF"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "The html is self-contained with ort and dict embedded; models (onnx) are loaded from IndexedDB via the UI (user uploads detection.onnx, cyrillic.onnx, cyrillic.txt). The user wants: \"встрой в html и отправь на гитхаб и сюда я скачаю и протестирую на телефоне\".\n\n\"встрой в html\" — likely means embed the models into the html too, so on the phone they just open one file without needing to upload models. Model sizes: detection 4.7MB gz 4.4, cyrillic 7.9MB gz 7.3 → b64gz ~15.6MB extra. The html is already 10MB. Total ~26MB. That's large but doable for phone. Alternatively they may just want the patched html pushed (already on the branch) and a downloadable copy in tmp/.\n\nGiven the phrase \"встрой в html\" (embed into html) right after our patch work — they probably want a single-file build with models embedded so they can test on the phone without manually importing 3 model files. The dict is already embedded; models are not. Let me check how models get into IndexedDB on first use — user imports files via the Models sheet. For phone testing that's painful. Embedding models as base64 gzip and auto-seeding IndexedDB on boot would make it self-contained.\n\nPlan:\n1. Add embedded model constants to koma-web.html: DET_GZ_B64, REC_GZ_B64 (cyrillic.txt dict is already embedded as DICT_GZ_B64; but model:dict key stores the text - we can reuse embeddedDictText for that).\n2. In boot, if DB has no model:det, seed from embedded constants (decompress gzip → ArrayBuffer → DB.put), then OCR.loadModels as usual.\n3. Bump version? The VERSION is 'v1.9.11'. Maybe bump to v1.9.12 with note. Let's bump to v1.9.12.\n4. Commit, push to the PR branch.\n5. Also produce a downloadable artifact: copy koma-web.html to /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai-web/tmp/ (files tab) — maybe named koma-web-v1.9.12.html. Also maybe attach to GitHub release for phone download.\n\nSize concern: embedding ~15.6MB base64 into html makes ~26MB file. Phone browsers can open a 26MB local html fine (it's just parse cost). The ort runtime is already embedded. Let's do it.\n\nHow to embed: generate JS constants with base64 of gzip. Insert near DICT_GZ_B64. Then boot seeding code.\n\nCheck DICT_GZ_B64 definition location and b64ToBytes. Also need to gunzip: they use DecompressionStream for dict. Same for models.\n\nMemory: converting base64 → bytes for 8MB model is fine.\n\nLet me find where DICT_GZ_B64 is declared to add the constants next to it.", "time": {"start": 1793037295672, "end": 1793037313078}, "id": "pr